#: gitswitch/mcp.py:23
msgid ""
"List the accounts Git-Switch manages, per host: the GitHub accounts the "
"GitHub CLI (gh) is logged in to and Forgejo, Gitea or GitLab accounts, "
"including which one is active and whether its token is still valid. Tokens "
"are never returned."
msgstr ""

#: gitswitch/mcp.py:33
msgid ""
"Switch the active account of a host: gh auth switch for GitHub, or the "
"account git uses for a Forgejo, Gitea or GitLab host. This applies to the "
"whole machine, not just this session. If the user enabled it in Git-Switch, "
"the global git user.name/user.email follow."
msgstr ""

#: gitswitch/mcp.py:40
msgid "Login name of the account to activate"
msgstr ""

#: gitswitch/mcp.py:43
msgid "Host name, only needed if the login exists on several hosts"
msgstr ""

#: gitswitch/mcp.py:53
msgid ""
"Read from the REST API of a Forgejo or Gitea server as the active account, "
"like 'gh api' for GitHub. The path is relative to /api/v1, for example /user/"
"repos, /repos/OWNER/NAME/issues?state=open, /repos/OWNER/NAME/pulls, /repos/"
"OWNER/NAME/releases, /repos/OWNER/NAME/actions/tasks or /repos/OWNER/NAME/"
"contents/PATH. Lists are paged with ?page= and ?limit=. The token is never "
"returned."
msgstr ""

#: gitswitch/mcp.py:61 gitswitch/mcp.py:81
msgid "API path below /api/v1, starting with /"
msgstr ""

#: gitswitch/mcp.py:62 gitswitch/mcp.py:83 gitswitch/mcp.py:102
#: gitswitch/mcp.py:123 gitswitch/mcp.py:144
msgid "Server, only needed if several are signed in"
msgstr ""

#: gitswitch/mcp.py:72
msgid ""
"Change something through the REST API of a Forgejo or Gitea server as the "
"active account: create or edit issues, comments, pull requests, releases and "
"repositories, merge a pull request (POST /repos/OWNER/NAME/pulls/INDEX/"
"merge), or sync a mirror (POST /repos/OWNER/NAME/mirror-sync). The path is "
"relative to /api/v1. DELETE requests remove data permanently."
msgstr ""

#: gitswitch/mcp.py:82 gitswitch/mcp.py:143
msgid "JSON body of the request"
msgstr ""

#: gitswitch/mcp.py:93
msgid ""
"Attach a local file to an existing release on a Forgejo or Gitea server. "
"Create the release first with forgejo_api_write (POST /repos/OWNER/NAME/"
"releases)."
msgstr ""

#: gitswitch/mcp.py:99
msgid "Repository as owner/name"
msgstr ""

#: gitswitch/mcp.py:100
msgid "Tag of the release"
msgstr ""

#: gitswitch/mcp.py:101
msgid "Path of the local file to upload"
msgstr ""

#: gitswitch/mcp.py:112
msgid ""
"Read from the REST API of a GitLab server as the active account, like 'gh "
"api' for GitHub. The path is relative to /api/v4, for example /user, /"
"projects?membership=true, /projects/OWNER%2FNAME/issues?state=opened, /"
"projects/OWNER%2FNAME/merge_requests, /projects/OWNER%2FNAME/pipelines or /"
"projects/OWNER%2FNAME/repository/files/PATH/raw?ref=main. Projects can be "
"addressed by ID or by their URL-encoded path. Lists are paged with ?page= "
"and ?per_page=. The token is never returned."
msgstr ""

#: gitswitch/mcp.py:122 gitswitch/mcp.py:142
msgid "API path below /api/v4, starting with /"
msgstr ""

#: gitswitch/mcp.py:133
msgid ""
"Change something through the REST API of a GitLab server as the active "
"account: create or edit issues, notes, merge requests, releases and "
"projects, merge a merge request (PUT /projects/OWNER%2FNAME/merge_requests/"
"IID/merge) or start a pipeline. The path is relative to /api/v4. DELETE "
"requests remove data permanently. Needs a token with the api scope."
msgstr ""

#: gitswitch/mcp.py:154
msgid ""
"Check content for private data before it is published: live tokens of the "
"signed-in accounts, other access tokens and private keys, addresses of the "
"user's self-hosted servers, the real git e-mail address, paths in the home "
"directory, the computer name and internal network addresses. Call it before "
"committing, pushing, creating a release, opening an issue or pull request, "
"or putting text into a README. Pass 'repository' to check what the next push "
"would publish, 'paths' for files or folders, or 'text' for a draft. Findings "
"of severity 'secret' must be removed; discuss 'private' and 'review' "
"findings with the user instead of publishing them."
msgstr ""

#: gitswitch/mcp.py:165
msgid "Text to check, for example a draft README or message"
msgstr ""

#: gitswitch/mcp.py:166
